Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/widget/ToastPresenter.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
ADR-0041 gap 4 (b4): the presenter takes no IAccessibilityManager and asks the process's AccessibilityManager.

Why: framework.jar has no IAccessibilityManager, as Minato runs no accessibility service (ADR-0041), and our
AccessibilityManager is the generated one of ADR-0045 decision 3, which answers that accessibility is off and has no
constructor over a service and no removeClient. The presenter sends its event only while accessibility is on, which it
never is, so a toast shows as on Android without one.

